---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Vetting a China Activewear Manufacturer: Trust Signals for High-Volume Buyers"
  description="Don't risk $30,000 on a middleman. Learn how to identify and verify a direct, high-capacity activewear factory in China."
>
  <article class="py-32 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-['Century_Gothic',sans-serif]">
    <header class="mb-16">
      <span class="text-accent font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">Industry Insights</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mt-4 mb-8 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">How to Vet a <span class="text-accent italic">China Activewear Factory</span></h1>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 text-gray-500 text-sm">
        <span>Published: June 19, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>10 Min Read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl text-black font-bold mb-8">For an experienced buyer, the biggest risk isn't quality—it's the supply chain. Is your "factory" actually a middleman with no control over production?</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">1. Verification of Vertically Integrated Production</h2>
      <p>A true high-volume partner should control everything from fabric sourcing to final packing. Ask for raw video footage of the production lines and the <strong>fabric R&D lab</strong>. At Fitclo, we welcome virtual live-stream tours of our 16,000㎡ Guangzhou facility and our additional plants in Dongguan and Yiwu (50,000㎡ total) to provide 100% transparency for our international partners.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">2. Financial and Operational Stability</h2>
      <p>A $30,000 order is a major commitment. Look for factories with a long history (we were founded in 2010) and a large workforce (over 350 employees). Small workshops often struggle with lead times and quality consistency during peak seasons.</p>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-8 rounded-3xl my-12">
        <h4 class="font-black text-black mb-4 uppercase text-sm">Top 3 "Red Flags" for B2B Buyers:</h4>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li>🚩 <strong>Vague Lead Times:</strong> If they can't give a specific 48-hour dispatch for stock, they don't own the stock.</li>
          <li>🚩 <strong>Lack of Certifications:</strong> A factory without ISO or SGS audits is a risk to your retail compliance.</li>
          <li>🚩 <strong>Limited Technical Knowledge:</strong> If they don't know the difference between interlock and single jersey knitting, they aren't manufacturers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">3. Scalability Proof</h2>
      <p>Ask for a "Capability Statement." This should list their monthly capacity (ours is 450,000 pieces) and the brands they've previously worked with. A factory that already serves the US/EU market understands the specific sizing and quality requirements of your region.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-20 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="bg-black text-white p-12 rounded-[40px] text-center">
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-6">Experience Transparency</h3>
        <p class="mb-8 text-white/70">Book a live virtual tour of the Fitclo manufacturing facility today.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-accent text-black px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-black uppercase tracking-widest hover:scale-105 transition-transform">Book Factory Tour</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
